IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV, "Administration": sections 97 to 102.
-- Who administers Part IV; the Income Tax Act provisions applied to amounts payable under it; cheques at financial
-- institutions; how a corporation signs; and section 102 (who may lay an information, the five-year limit, and the rules of
-- evidence and proof for prosecutions and proceedings under the Part).
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- The Income Tax Act, the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and the Companies' Creditors
-- Arrangement Act are not among the inputs: where a section applies one of their provisions, the rule says that the provision
-- applies (a BOOLEAN) and does not restate what the provision does.
-- An evidentiary rule ("is evidence of", "is deemed") is encoded as the condition under which the evidence or deeming arises.

§ `Section 97 - administration`

-- "The Minister shall administer this Part, section 5, subsections 152.01(2) and (3) and sections 152.21 to 152.3 and any regulations
-- made under sections 5, 55, 152.26 and 152.28": in Part IV, "Minister" is the Minister of National Revenue (the keel's `Party`).
-- src:1618 | 97 (1) The Minister shall administer this Part, section 5, subsections 152.01(2) and (3) and sections 152.21 to 152.3 and any regulations made under sections 5, 55, 152.26 and 152.28, and the Commissioner of Revenue may exercise all the powers and perform all the duties of the Minister under this Part and Part VII.1.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 97(1) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the matter is this Part, section 5, subsection 152.01(2) or (3), any of sections 152.21 to 152.3, or regulations made under section 5, 55, 152.26 or 152.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
DECIDE `s 97(1) who administers the matter` IS
    IF `the matter is this Part, section 5, subsection 152.01(2) or (3), any of sections 152.21 to 152.3, or regulations made under section 5, 55, 152.26 or 152.28`
    THEN JUST `the Minister of National Revenue`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The Commissioner of Revenue may exercise all the powers and perform all the duties of the Minister under this Part and Part VII.1."
-- src:1618 | 97 (1) The Minister shall administer this Part, section 5, subsections 152.01(2) and (3) and sections 152.21 to 152.3 and any regulations made under sections 5, 55, 152.26 and 152.28, and the Commissioner of Revenue may exercise all the powers and perform all the duties of the Minister under this Part and Part VII.1.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 97(1) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the powers or duties are the Minister's under this Part or Part VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 97(1) the Commissioner of Revenue may exercise the power and perform the duty` IF
    `the powers or duties are the Minister's under this Part or Part VII.1`

-- Subsection (2): an officer or employee employed in the administration of those provisions, if designated by the Minister for
-- the purpose, may in the course of their employment administer oaths and take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations
-- for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of the Act or the regulations; and has for those
-- purposes all the powers of a commissioner for administering oaths or taking affidavits.
-- src:1620 | (2) An officer or employee employed in connection with the administration of this Part, section 5, subsection 152.01(2) or (3) or any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or any regulations made under section 5, 55, 152.26 or 152.28, if designated by the Minister for the purpose, may, in the course of their employment, administer oaths and take and receive affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of this Act or the regulations, and every officer or employee so designated has for those purposes all the powers of a commissioner for administering oaths or taking affidavits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 97(2) (src:1620)
GIVEN `is an officer or employee employed in connection with the administration of this Part, section 5, subsection 152.01(2) or (3), any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or regulations made under section 5, 55, 152.26 or 152.28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is designated by the Minister for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts in the course of their employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 97(2) the officer or employee may administer oaths and take and receive affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations` IF
        `is an officer or employee employed in connection with the administration of this Part, section 5, subsection 152.01(2) or (3), any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or regulations made under section 5, 55, 152.26 or 152.28`
    AND `is designated by the Minister for the purpose`
    AND `acts in the course of their employment`
    AND `acts for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of this Act or the regulations`

-- src:1620 | (2) An officer or employee employed in connection with the administration of this Part, section 5, subsection 152.01(2) or (3) or any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or any regulations made under section 5, 55, 152.26 or 152.28, if designated by the Minister for the purpose, may, in the course of their employment, administer oaths and take and receive affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of this Act or the regulations, and every officer or employee so designated has for those purposes all the powers of a commissioner for administering oaths or taking affidavits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 97(2) (src:1620)
GIVEN `is an officer or employee so designated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 97(2) the officer or employee has all the powers of a commissioner for administering oaths or taking affidavits` IF
        `is an officer or employee so designated`
    AND `acts for the purposes of or incidental to the administration or enforcement of this Act or the regulations`

§ `Sections 98 and 99 - Income Tax Act provisions`

-- src:1622 | 98 (1) Section 223 of the Income Tax Act applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in relation to amounts payable under this Part that have not been paid and to any parts of amounts payable under this Part that have not been paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 98(1) (src:1622)
GIVEN `the amount is payable under this Part and has not been paid, or is a part of such an amount that has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 98(1) section 223 of the Income Tax Act applies to the amount` IF
    `the amount is payable under this Part and has not been paid, or is a part of such an amount that has not been paid`

-- Subsection (2): (1) applies to (a) certificates made by the Minister of National Revenue under (1), or under section 79 of the
-- Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, AFTER January 1, 1972; and (b) documents evidencing the certificates, issued by the
-- Federal Court and filed, registered or otherwise recorded AFTER 1977 (the year 1978 or later). "Subject to subsection (3)."
-- src:1624 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), subsection (1) applies with respect to
-- src:1625 | (a) certificates made by the Minister of National Revenue under subsection (1), or under section 79 of the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, chapter 48 of the Statutes of Canada, 1970-71-72, after January 1, 1972; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 98(2)(a) (src:1624-1625)
GIVEN `the day on which the certificate was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 98(2)(a) subsection (1) applies with respect to the certificate` IF
    `the day on which the certificate was made` GREATER THAN (YMD 1972 1 1)

-- src:1624 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), subsection (1) applies with respect to
-- src:1625 | (a) certificates made by the Minister of National Revenue under subsection (1), or under section 79 of the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, chapter 48 of the Statutes of Canada, 1970-71-72, after January 1, 1972; and
-- src:1626 | (b) documents evidencing the certificates that were issued by the Federal Court and that were filed, registered or otherwise recorded after 1977 under the laws of a province.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 98(2)(b) (src:1624) (src:1626)
GIVEN `the year in which the document evidencing the certificate was filed, registered or otherwise recorded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 98(2)(b) subsection (1) applies with respect to the document` IF
    `the year in which the document evidencing the certificate was filed, registered or otherwise recorded` GREATER THAN 1977

-- Subsection (3): if the certificate or document was the subject of an action pending in a court on February 10, 1988, or of a
-- court decision given on or before that date, section 79 of the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, as it read immediately
-- before September 13, 1988, continues to apply to it.
-- src:1628 | (3) If the certificate or document was the subject of an action pending in a court on February 10, 1988 or of a court decision given on or before that date, section 79 of the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, chapter 48 of the Statutes of Canada, 1970-71-72, as it read immediately before September 13, 1988, continues to apply with respect to that certificate or document.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 98(3) (src:1628)
GIVEN `the certificate or document was the subject of an action pending in a court on February 10, 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the court decision on it, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 98(3) section 79 of the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, as it read immediately before September 13, 1988, continues to apply` IF
        `the certificate or document was the subject of an action pending in a court on February 10, 1988`
    OR  (CONSIDER `the day of the court decision on it, if there was one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST decidedOn THEN decidedOn AT MOST (YMD 1988 2 10))

-- src:1630 | 99 Section 160, subsections 161(11) and 220(3.1), sections 221.1 and 224 to 224.3 and subsections 227(9.1) and (10) and 248(7) and (11) of the Income Tax Act apply to all premiums, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a person under this Part and Part VII.1, with the modifications that the circumstances require, and for the purposes of this section,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 99 (src:1630)
GIVEN `the amount is a premium, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Part or Part VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 99 the listed provisions of the Income Tax Act apply to the amount` IF
    `the amount is a premium, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Part or Part VII.1`

-- Paragraph (a): the reference in subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act to "subsection 227(10.1) or a similar provision" is
-- read as a reference to "section 85 or 152.24, as the case may be, of the Employment Insurance Act". The converted text shows
-- "152. 24" with a stray space; it is read as section 152.24 (NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say").
-- src:1631 | (a) the reference in subsection 224(1.2) of that Act to “subsection 227(10.1) or a similar provision” is to be read as a reference to “section 85 or 152. 24, as the case may be, of the Employment Insurance Act”; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 99(a) (src:1631)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 99(a) the reference in subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act to "subsection 227(10.1) or a similar provision" is read as a reference to` MEANS
    "section 85 or 152.24, as the case may be, of the Employment Insurance Act"

-- Paragraph (b): subsection 224(1.2) applies to employer's premiums, employee's premiums and Part VII.1 premiums and related
-- interest, penalties or other amounts, subject to subsections 69(1) and 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and
-- section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act.
-- src:1632 | (b) subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act applies to employer’s premiums, employee’s premiums, and premiums under Part VII.1, and related interest, penalties or other amounts, subject to subsections 69(1) and 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and section 11.09 of the Companies’ Creditors Arrangement Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 99(b) (src:1632)
GIVEN `the amount is an employer's premium, an employee's premium or a premium under Part VII.1, or related interest, penalties or other amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case falls within subsection 69(1) or 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 99(b) subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act applies to the amount` IF
        `the amount is an employer's premium, an employee's premium or a premium under Part VII.1, or related interest, penalties or other amounts`
    AND (NOT `the case falls within subsection 69(1) or 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act`)

§ `Sections 100 and 101 - cheques, corporations`

-- src:1634 | 100 A financial institution shall receive for deposit, without charge for discount or commission, a cheque made payable to the Receiver General in payment of premiums, interest or penalties imposed by this Part, whether drawn on the financial institution receiving the cheque or on any other financial institution in Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 100 (src:1634)
GIVEN `the cheque is made payable to the Receiver General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in payment of premiums, interest or penalties imposed by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is drawn on the financial institution receiving it or on any other financial institution in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 100 the financial institution shall receive the cheque for deposit without charge for discount or commission` IF
        `the cheque is made payable to the Receiver General`
    AND `it is in payment of premiums, interest or penalties imposed by this Part`
    AND `it is drawn on the financial institution receiving it or on any other financial institution in Canada`

-- src:1636 | 101 A return, certificate or other document made by a corporation under this Part or the regulations shall be signed for it by the president, secretary or treasurer of the corporation or by any other officer or person duly authorized by the board of directors or other governing body of the corporation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 101 (src:1636)
GIVEN `the document is a return, certificate or other document made by a corporation under this Part or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the president, secretary or treasurer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by another officer or person duly authorized by the board of directors or other governing body of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 101 the document is signed for the corporation as required` IF
        `the document is a return, certificate or other document made by a corporation under this Part or the regulations`
    AND (`it is signed by the president, secretary or treasurer of the corporation` OR `it is signed by another officer or person duly authorized by the board of directors or other governing body of the corporation`)

§ `Section 102(1) to (4) - informations and complaints`

-- src:1638 | 102 (1) An information or complaint under this Part may be laid or made by an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, by a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or by an authorized person and, if an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Part, it is deemed to have been laid or made by an authorized person and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(1) (src:1638)
GIVEN `is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(1) the person may lay or make an information or complaint under this Part` IF
        `is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    OR  `is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police`
    OR  `is an authorized person`

-- "If an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Part, it is deemed to have been laid or made by an
-- authorized person and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the
-- Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty."
-- src:1638 | 102 (1) An information or complaint under this Part may be laid or made by an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, by a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or by an authorized person and, if an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Part, it is deemed to have been laid or made by an authorized person and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(1) (src:1638)
GIVEN `an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(1) the information or complaint is deemed to have been laid or made by an authorized person` IF
    `an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Part`

-- src:1638 | 102 (1) An information or complaint under this Part may be laid or made by an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, by a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or by an authorized person and, if an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Part, it is deemed to have been laid or made by an authorized person and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(1) (src:1638)
GIVEN `the person calling it into question is the Minister or a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(1) the information or complaint may be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant` IF
    `the person calling it into question is the Minister or a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty`

-- Subsection (2): no proceeding is "objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences". For any other ground
-- the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1640 | (2) An information or complaint about an offence under this Part may be for one or more offences and no information, complaint, warrant, conviction or other proceeding in a prosecution under this Part is objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(2) (src:1640)
GIVEN `the ground of objection is that it relates to two or more offences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(2) the information, complaint, warrant, conviction or other proceeding is objectionable or insufficient` IS
    IF `the ground of objection is that it relates to two or more offences`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1642 | (3) An information or complaint about an offence under this Part may be heard, tried or determined by a provincial court judge, as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, if the accused is resident, carrying on business, found, apprehended or in custody within the judge’s territorial jurisdiction although the matter of the information or complaint did not arise within that jurisdiction.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(3) (src:1642)
GIVEN `the accused is resident within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is carrying on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(3) a provincial court judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the jurisdiction` IF
        `the accused is resident within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
    OR  `the accused is carrying on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
    OR  `the accused is found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
    OR  `the accused is apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
    OR  `the accused is in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`

-- Subsection (4): "within five years after the subject-matter of the information or complaint arose": that day is not counted, the
-- fifth anniversary is the last day (`add years`, which clamps 29 February to 28 February; fork F-ei3-23).
-- src:1644 | (4) An information or complaint for an offence under this Part may be laid or made within five years after the subject-matter of the information or complaint arose.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(4) (src:1644)
GIVEN `the day on which the subject-matter of the information or complaint arose` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the information or complaint is laid or made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(4) the information or complaint is laid or made in time` IF
    `the day on which the information or complaint is laid or made` AT MOST (`add years` `the day on which the subject-matter of the information or complaint arose` 5)

§ `Section 102(5) to (19) - proof and presumptions`

-- (5) Proof of service by mail: where the Part or the regulations provide for sending a request, notice or demand by mail, an
-- affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating (a), (b), (c) is evidence of the request, notice or demand and of
-- its being sent.
-- src:1646 | (5) If provision is made by this Part or the regulations for sending by mail a request for information, notice or demand, an affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1647 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case,
-- src:1648 | (b) such a request, notice or demand was sent by registered letter on a named day to the person to whom it was addressed, indicating the address, and
-- src:1649 | (c) the officer identifies as exhibits attached to the affidavit the post office certificate of registration of the letter or a true copy of the relevant portion of the certificate and a true copy of the request, notice or demand,
-- src:1650 | is evidence of the request, notice or demand and of its being sent.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(5) (src:1646-1650)
GIVEN `provision is made by this Part or the regulations for sending the request, notice or demand by mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the request, notice or demand was sent by registered letter on a named day to the person to whom it was addressed, indicating the address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies as exhibits the post office certificate of registration of the letter or a true copy of the relevant portion of it and a true copy of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(5) the affidavit is evidence of the request, notice or demand and of its being sent` IF
        `provision is made by this Part or the regulations for sending the request, notice or demand by mail`
    AND `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
    AND `it states that the request, notice or demand was sent by registered letter on a named day to the person to whom it was addressed, indicating the address`
    AND `it identifies as exhibits the post office certificate of registration of the letter or a true copy of the relevant portion of it and a true copy of the request, notice or demand`

-- src:1652 | (6) If provision is made by this Part or the regulations for personal service of a request for information, notice or demand, an affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1653 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case,
-- src:1654 | (b) such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed, and
-- src:1655 | (c) the officer identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand,
-- src:1656 | is evidence of the request, notice or demand and of its personal service.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(6) (src:1652-1656)
GIVEN `provision is made by this Part or the regulations for personal service of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies as an exhibit a true copy of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(6) the affidavit is evidence of the request, notice or demand and of its personal service` IF
        `provision is made by this Part or the regulations for personal service of the request, notice or demand`
    AND `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
    AND `it states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed`
    AND `it identifies as an exhibit a true copy of the request, notice or demand`

-- src:1658 | (7) If a person is required by this Part or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate, an affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1659 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1660 | (b) after a careful examination and search of the records the officer has been unable to find in a given case that the return, statement, answer or certificate, as the case may be, has been filed or made by the person,
-- src:1661 | is evidence that the person did not do so in that case.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(7) (src:1658-1661)
GIVEN `a person is required by this Part or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that after a careful examination and search of the records the officer has been unable to find in the given case that it has been filed or made by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(7) the affidavit is evidence that the person did not file or make it` IF
        `a person is required by this Part or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate`
    AND `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `it states that after a careful examination and search of the records the officer has been unable to find in the given case that it has been filed or made by the person`

-- src:1663 | (8) If a person is required by this Part or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate, an affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1664 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1665 | (b) after careful examination of the records the officer has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day,
-- src:1666 | is evidence that it was filed or made on that day and not before.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(8) (src:1663-1666)
GIVEN `a person is required by this Part or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that after careful examination of the records the officer has found that it was filed or made on a particular day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(8) the affidavit is evidence that it was filed or made on that day and not before` IF
        `a person is required by this Part or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate`
    AND `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `it states that after careful examination of the records the officer has found that it was filed or made on a particular day`

-- src:1668 | (9) An affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1669 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1670 | (b) a document annexed to it is a document or true copy of a document made by or for an employer, the Minister or a person exercising the powers of the Minister,
-- src:1671 | is evidence of the nature and contents of the document and is admissible in evidence and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(9) (src:1668-1671)
GIVEN `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that a document annexed to it is a document or true copy of a document made by or for an employer, the Minister or a person exercising the powers of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(9) the affidavit is evidence of the nature and contents of the document, admissible, with the same probative force as the original` IF
        `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `it states that a document annexed to it is a document or true copy of a document made by or for an employer, the Minister or a person exercising the powers of the Minister`

-- src:1673 | (10) An affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1674 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the practice of the Agency,
-- src:1675 | (b) an examination of the records shows that a notice of assessment for a particular year was mailed or otherwise communicated to an employer on a particular day under this Part, and
-- src:1676 | (c) after careful examination and search of the records, the officer has been unable to find that a notice of appeal from the assessment was received within the time allowed,
-- src:1677 | is evidence of the statements contained in it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(10) (src:1673-1677)
GIVEN `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the practice of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that an examination of the records shows that a notice of assessment for a particular year was mailed or otherwise communicated to an employer on a particular day under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that after careful examination and search of the records the officer has been unable to find that a notice of appeal from the assessment was received within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(10) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` IF
        `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the practice of the Agency`
    AND `it states that an examination of the records shows that a notice of assessment for a particular year was mailed or otherwise communicated to an employer on a particular day under this Part`
    AND `it states that after careful examination and search of the records the officer has been unable to find that a notice of appeal from the assessment was received within the time allowed`

-- (11) Presumption: where evidence is offered under s 102 by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making it is an
-- officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, it is not necessary to prove (a) the person's signature, (b) that the person is such an
-- officer, or (c) the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn. For any other matter
-- the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
DECLARE `ei3 Matter an affidavit may leave unproved` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 the signature of the person making the affidavit`
    `ei3 that the person making the affidavit is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    `ei3 the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn`
    `ei3 any other matter`

-- src:1679 | (11) If evidence is offered under this section by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making the affidavit is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, it is not necessary to prove
-- src:1680 | (a) the person’s signature;
-- src:1681 | (b) that the person is such an officer; or
-- src:1682 | (c) the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(11) (src:1679-1682)
GIVEN `evidence is offered under this section by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making it is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `ei3 Matter an affidavit may leave unproved`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(11) it is necessary to prove the matter` IS
    IF `evidence is offered under this section by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making it is an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    THEN (CONSIDER matter
          WHEN `ei3 any other matter` THEN NOTHING
          OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1684 | (12) Judicial notice shall be taken of all orders made under this Part without the orders being specially pleaded or proven.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(12) (src:1684)
GIVEN `the order is made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(12) judicial notice shall be taken of the order without it being specially pleaded or proven` IF
    `the order is made under this Part`

-- (13) A document appearing to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision, assessment, discharge of
-- mortgage, release of hypothec or other document executed under or in the course of administering or enforcing this Part, over the
-- name in writing of the Minister, the Deputy Minister of National Revenue, the Commissioner of Customs and Revenue, the
-- Commissioner of Revenue or an officer authorized to exercise the Minister's powers, is deemed to be signed, made and issued by
-- that person unless called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
-- src:1686 | (13) Every document appearing to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision, assessment, discharge of mortgage, release of hypothec or other document executed under, or in the course of the administration or enforcement of, this Part over the name in writing of the Minister, the Deputy Minister of National Revenue, the Commissioner of Customs and Revenue, the Commissioner of Revenue or an officer authorized to exercise the powers or perform the duties of the Minister under this Part, is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by the Minister, the Deputy Minister, the Commissioner of Customs and Revenue, the Commissioner of Revenue or the officer unless it has been called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(13) (src:1686)
GIVEN `the document appears to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision, assessment, discharge of mortgage, release of hypothec or other document executed under, or in the course of the administration or enforcement of, this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is over the name in writing of the Minister, the Deputy Minister of National Revenue, the Commissioner of Customs and Revenue, the Commissioner of Revenue or an officer authorized to exercise the powers or perform the duties of the Minister under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(13) the document is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by that person` IF
        `the document appears to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision, assessment, discharge of mortgage, release of hypothec or other document executed under, or in the course of the administration or enforcement of, this Part`
    AND `it is over the name in writing of the Minister, the Deputy Minister of National Revenue, the Commissioner of Customs and Revenue, the Commissioner of Revenue or an officer authorized to exercise the powers or perform the duties of the Minister under this Part`
    AND (NOT `it has been called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty`)

-- (14) The assessment is deemed to have been made on the day the notice of assessment is sent.
-- src:1688 | (14) If a notice of assessment has been sent by the Minister as required by this Part, the assessment is deemed to have been made on the day on which the notice is sent.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(14) (src:1688)
GIVEN `a notice of assessment has been sent by the Minister as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the notice is sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 102(14) the day on which the assessment is deemed to have been made` IS
    IF `a notice of assessment has been sent by the Minister as required by this Part`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the notice is sent`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1690 | (15) A form that appears to be authorized by the Minister is deemed to be a form authorized by the Minister under this Part unless called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(15) (src:1690)
GIVEN `the form appears to be authorized by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(15) the form is deemed to be a form authorized by the Minister under this Part` IF
        `the form appears to be authorized by the Minister`
    AND (NOT `it has been called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty`)

-- (16) In a prosecution for an offence under this Part, the production of a return, certificate, statement or answer required
-- by or under the Part or the regulations, appearing to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged, or to have been
-- made or signed by or for the person, is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that it was.
-- src:1692 | (16) In a prosecution for an offence under this Part, the production of a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under this Part or the regulations, appearing to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged with the offence or to have been made or signed by or for the person is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the return, certificate, statement or answer was filed or delivered by or for that person or was made or signed by or for the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(16) (src:1692)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return, certificate, statement or answer is required by or under this Part or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is produced and appears to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged, or to have been made or signed by or for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(16) the production is proof that it was filed, delivered, made or signed by or for the person charged` IF
        `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Part`
    AND `the return, certificate, statement or answer is required by or under this Part or the regulations`
    AND `it is produced and appears to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged, or to have been made or signed by or for the person`
    AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)

-- src:1694 | (17) In any proceedings before the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada under section 104, the production of a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under this Part or the regulations, appearing to have been filed or delivered by or for an employer or to have been made or signed by or for the employer is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the return, certificate, statement or answer was filed or delivered by or for the employer or was made or signed by or for the employer.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(17) (src:1694)
GIVEN `the proceeding is before the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada under section 104` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return, certificate, statement or answer is required by or under this Part or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is produced and appears to have been filed or delivered by or for an employer, or to have been made or signed by or for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(17) the production is proof that it was filed, delivered, made or signed by or for the employer` IF
        `the proceeding is before the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada under section 104`
    AND `the return, certificate, statement or answer is required by or under this Part or the regulations`
    AND `it is produced and appears to have been filed or delivered by or for an employer, or to have been made or signed by or for the employer`
    AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)

-- src:1696 | (18) In a prosecution for an offence under this Act, an affidavit of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency stating that
-- src:1697 | (a) the officer has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1698 | (b) an examination of the records shows that an amount required under this Act to be remitted to the Receiver General on account of premiums has not been received by the Receiver General,
-- src:1699 | is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(18) (src:1696-1699)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that an examination of the records shows that an amount required under this Act to be remitted to the Receiver General on account of premiums has not been received by the Receiver General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(18) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` IF
        `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act`
    AND `the affidavit is of an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND `it states that the officer has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `it states that an examination of the records shows that an amount required under this Act to be remitted to the Receiver General on account of premiums has not been received by the Receiver General`

-- (19) Partnerships. (a) A reference to the firm name of a partnership is read as a reference to all its members.
-- (b) A notice or document is deemed provided to each member if it is mailed to, served on or otherwise sent to the partnership
-- (i) at its latest known address or place of business, or (ii) at the latest known address (A) of any member whose liability is not
-- limited, if it is a limited partnership, or (B) of any member, in any other case.
-- src:1701 | (19) For the purposes of this Part,
-- src:1702 | (a) a reference in a notice or other document to the firm name of a partnership shall be read as a reference to all its members; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(19)(a) (src:1701-1702)
GIVEN `a reference in a notice or other document is to the firm name of a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(19)(a) the reference is read as a reference to all the members of the partnership` IF
    `a reference in a notice or other document is to the firm name of a partnership`

-- src:1701 | (19) For the purposes of this Part,
-- src:1702 | (a) a reference in a notice or other document to the firm name of a partnership shall be read as a reference to all its members; and
-- src:1703 | (b) a notice or other document is deemed to have been provided to each member of a partnership if it is mailed to, served on or otherwise sent to the partnership
-- src:1704 | (i) at its latest known address or place of business, or
-- src:1705 | (ii) at the latest known address
-- src:1706 | (A) if it is a limited partnership, of any member of the partnership whose liability as a member is not limited, or
-- src:1707 | (B) in any other case, of any member of the partnership.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 102(19)(b) (src:1701) (src:1703-1707)
GIVEN `the notice or other document is mailed to, served on or otherwise sent to the partnership at its latest known address or place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partnership is a limited partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent at the latest known address of a member whose liability as a member is not limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent at the latest known address of any member of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 102(19)(b) the notice or other document is deemed to have been provided to each member of the partnership` IF
        `the notice or other document is mailed to, served on or otherwise sent to the partnership at its latest known address or place of business`
    OR  (IF `the partnership is a limited partnership`
         THEN `it is sent at the latest known address of a member whose liability as a member is not limited`
         ELSE `it is sent at the latest known address of any member of the partnership`)
